{
  "title": "WooCommerce \u2014 ecommerce (10,303\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: WooCommerce\nDomain: ecommerce | Scale: large | Stars: 10,303\nProblem: Provides a customizable, open-source ecommerce platform built on WordPress that enables merchants to build any commerce solution. Serves as the foundation for online stores and ecommerce extensions.\nTarget users: WordPress site owners and merchants, Ecommerce developers and agencies, Extension developers, Enterprise retailers\nCore features: Customizable product management and catalog; Shopping cart and checkout functionality; Payment gateway integrations; Order management and fulfillment; Extensible plugin architecture with marketplace; Admin dashboard and reporting; Customer management and accounts\nIntegrations: WordPress ecosystem, Payment processors (Stripe, PayPal, etc.), Shipping providers, Tax calculation services, WooCommerce extensions marketplace\nTech stack: React, TypeScript, JavaScript, SCSS + PHP 7.4+ + WordPress database (MySQL/MariaDB) + WordPress hosting compatible\nKey libraries: React, TypeScript, Webpack, Babel, Jest, Composer, PNPM\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure (plugins, packages, tools) enables modular development while maintaining core plugin cohesion\n- Dual language approach (PHP backend + React frontend) allows gradual modernization of legacy WordPress code\n- Workspace-based dependency management with PNPM enables consistent versioning across 50+ interconnected packages\n- Plugin-based extensibility pattern allows third-party developers to build on core platform without forking",
